<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-16T18:50:45+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:50:45 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Centre expands Census enumerator pool to include private school teachers, clerks]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-expands-census-enumerator-pool-to-include-private-school-teachers-clerks/articleshow/134995981.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134995981.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Under the amended rules, teachers working in educational institutions run by the government, local authorities, aided or unaided private bodies, societies and trusts can be appointed as enumerators. The eligibility list also covers clerks and other officials working for the Central and state governments, local authorities and various establishments. The Census Rules were first published in the Gazette of India on December 31, 1990.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-expands-census-enumerator-pool-to-include-private-school-teachers-clerks/articleshow/134995981.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-expands-census-enumerator-pool-to-include-private-school-teachers-clerks/articleshow/134995981.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:38:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134996160,imgsize-99152.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Police can break bones, not satyagraha’: Rahul Gandhi alleges Delhi Police refused to file FIR over assault on student protesters]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-can-break-bones-not-satyagraha-rahul-gandhi-alleges-delhi-police-refused-to-file-fir-over-assault-on-student-protesters/articleshow/134995636.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134995636.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi alleged that Delhi Police failed to register an FIR regarding the assault on student protesters. He mentioned two young women were among those harmed, prompting legal action against police officers. Detentions occurred ahead of a proposed Tiranga rally in Connaught Place, highlighting increased security measures in the area. Police cited restrictions and prior agreements while detaining activists to maintain public order.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-can-break-bones-not-satyagraha-rahul-gandhi-alleges-delhi-police-refused-to-file-fir-over-assault-on-student-protesters/articleshow/134995636.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/police-can-break-bones-not-satyagraha-rahul-gandhi-alleges-delhi-police-refused-to-file-fir-over-assault-on-student-protesters/articleshow/134995636.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:28:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134995904,imgsize-57824.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Valid ID cards, 'impartial' reporting, basic first-aid: Press Council issues guidelines for journalists covering anti-SIR protests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/valid-id-cards-impartial-reporting-basic-first-aid-press-council-issues-guidelines-for-journalists-covering-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134994945.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994945.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/valid-id-cards-impartial-reporting-basic-first-aid-press-council-issues-guidelines-for-journalists-covering-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134994945.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/valid-id-cards-impartial-reporting-basic-first-aid-press-council-issues-guidelines-for-journalists-covering-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134994945.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T18:13:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134995523,imgsize-222924.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MEA confirms Jaishankar-Rubio talks in Mumbai after Rahul’s jibe over India visit]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-confirms-jaishankar-rubio-talks-in-mumbai-after-rahuls-jibe-over-india-visit/articleshow/134994627.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134994627.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[MEA spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal announced the engagements while responding to a question from news agency ANI about whether Jaishankar was expected to hold any meetings in Mumbai next week. He also explained that hosting foreign dignitaries outside the national capital was not unusual, pointing to previous engagements held in different Indian cities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-confirms-jaishankar-rubio-talks-in-mumbai-after-rahuls-jibe-over-india-visit/articleshow/134994627.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-confirms-jaishankar-rubio-talks-in-mumbai-after-rahuls-jibe-over-india-visit/articleshow/134994627.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:51:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994937,imgsize-42440.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Ensure safety of Indian nationals’: MEA’s strong message to US after alleged Hindu temple attack plot]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ensure-safety-of-indian-nationals-meas-strong-message-to-us-after-alleged-hindu-temple-attack-plot/articleshow/134993812.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993812.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Authorities in Aurora thwarted a disturbing mass-shooting scheme aimed at a local Hindu temple. In light of this, the Indian ministry of external affairs voiced alarm over the rise in hate crimes in the United States. A 19-year-old suspect now faces charges for threatening the temple while armed. Meanwhile, Indian-American organizations are mobilizing to spotlight anti-Indian sentiment and exploring collective response strategies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ensure-safety-of-indian-nationals-meas-strong-message-to-us-after-alleged-hindu-temple-attack-plot/articleshow/134993812.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ensure-safety-of-indian-nationals-meas-strong-message-to-us-after-alleged-hindu-temple-attack-plot/articleshow/134993812.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:40:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994603,imgsize-96196.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening newswrap: CJP's Dipke detained, Rajnath alleges regime change bid and Rahul's cryptic Rubio post]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-cjps-dipke-detained-rajnath-alleges-regime-change-bid-and-rahuls-cryptic-rubio-post/articleshow/134992924.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992924.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-cjps-dipke-detained-rajnath-alleges-regime-change-bid-and-rahuls-cryptic-rubio-post/articleshow/134992924.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-cjps-dipke-detained-rajnath-alleges-regime-change-bid-and-rahuls-cryptic-rubio-post/articleshow/134992924.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:37:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134994488,imgsize-84225.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I am alone': CJP's Dipke argues with cops during detention ahead of Tiranga march - watch]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-am-alone-cjps-dipke-argues-with-cops-during-detention-ahead-of-tiranga-march-watch/articleshow/134993030.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993030.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Dipke, earlier today, had defended the party's protests, asserting that peaceful demonstrations were a democratic right. He accused the government of restricting citizens' freedoms and disrupting business activities through shutdowns, Internet suspensions and movement restrictions. "I'm alone, what law did I break," Dipke asked before he was detained. The court had directed the CJP to refrain from causing any public disturbance for a period of one year.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-am-alone-cjps-dipke-argues-with-cops-during-detention-ahead-of-tiranga-march-watch/articleshow/134993030.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-am-alone-cjps-dipke-argues-with-cops-during-detention-ahead-of-tiranga-march-watch/articleshow/134993030.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:07:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134993455,imgsize-60528.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ladakh administration announces Sankoo as eighth district]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ladakh-administration-announces-sankoo-as-eighth-district/articleshow/134993240.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134993240.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The authorities in Ladakh have announced the formation of Sankoo as its eighth district, fulfilling a long-awaited aspiration. Lieutenant Governor V K Saxena underscored this decision as part of the government's commitment to progress. Various local organizations, notably Anjuman-e-Sahib Zaman led by Syed Mohammad Razvi, played a crucial role in this development.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ladakh-administration-announces-sankoo-as-eighth-district/articleshow/134993240.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ladakh-administration-announces-sankoo-as-eighth-district/articleshow/134993240.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T17:02:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134993405,imgsize-94820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Protesters ignorant of ground realities': Delhi traders write to PM Modi over losses]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protesters-ignorant-of-ground-realities-delhi-traders-write-to-pm-modi-over-losses/articleshow/134992421.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992421.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The traders urged the authorities to ensure a transparent assessment of the losses suffered by shopkeepers following the October 10 protest and recover full compensation from the principal organisers and participants responsible, rather than place the financial burden on traders already struggling with lost business. It said shop earnings supported traders' families and employees, while covering shop rents, children's education and medical expenses for elderly parents.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protesters-ignorant-of-ground-realities-delhi-traders-write-to-pm-modi-over-losses/articleshow/134992421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protesters-ignorant-of-ground-realities-delhi-traders-write-to-pm-modi-over-losses/articleshow/134992421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T16:47:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134992951,imgsize-186926.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Regime change’ remark row: BJP chief Nitin Nabin says opposition’s ‘true agenda’ exposed]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/regime-change-remark-row-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-says-oppositions-true-agenda-exposed/articleshow/134992022.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134992022.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/regime-change-remark-row-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-says-oppositions-true-agenda-exposed/articleshow/134992022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/regime-change-remark-row-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-says-oppositions-true-agenda-exposed/articleshow/134992022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T16:43:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134992808,imgsize-39254.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't try to bulldoze another Constitutional Amendment Bill': Kharge writes to PM Modi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-try-to-bulldoze-another-constitutional-amendment-bill-kharge-writes-to-pm-modi/articleshow/134990356.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134990356.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-try-to-bulldoze-another-constitutional-amendment-bill-kharge-writes-to-pm-modi/articleshow/134990356.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-try-to-bulldoze-another-constitutional-amendment-bill-kharge-writes-to-pm-modi/articleshow/134990356.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T1